# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AlphaEngine research portal — data provider keys.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev, or add in Vercel → Settings → Environment
# Variables for a deployment. EVERY key is optional: with none set, crypto
# quotes/bars/depth still work through Binance's public endpoints. Each key you
# add lights up more capability — nothing else changes.
#
# GET /api/providers shows, per capability, exactly which of these are live and
# how much of each free-tier quota the running instance has spent.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Financial Modeling Prep — equity quotes (primary), fundamentals (primary),
# daily bars, news. Free: 250 req/day.       https://financialmodelingprep.com
FMP_API_KEY=

# Tiingo — IEX equity quotes, EOD/intraday bars, crypto, news archive.
# Free: 1,000 req/day (personal use).        https://www.tiingo.com
TIINGO_API_KEY=

# Massive (formerly Polygon.io) — equity/crypto aggregates (primary for bars),
# reference data, news. Free: 5 req/min, EOD.       https://massive.com
MASSIVE_API_KEY=
# Point at the legacy host if your key predates the rebrand:
# MASSIVE_BASE_URL=https://api.polygon.io

# Alpha Vantage — quotes, bars, fundamentals, news WITH sentiment scores.
# Free: 25 req/day (ranked last everywhere by arithmetic).
#                              https://www.alphavantage.co/support/#api-key
ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=

# Firecrawl — open-web search + page-to-markdown for filings, exchange
# notices, protocol announcements. Free: 1,000 credits/month.
#                                                  https://www.firecrawl.dev
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# OpenBB — deploy the included stateless `OpenBB_Service/` independently, then
# point this server-only URL at its stable HTTPS origin. The service has no
# portfolio, order, Telegram, or web-UI responsibilities.
OPENBB_API_URL=
# Use the same long random value configured as OPENBB_API_TOKEN on that service.
OPENBB_API_TOKEN=

# Optional connection to the included FastAPI risk gateway. The browser calls a
# same-origin read-only proxy; this URL and token remain server-side. Reliability
# reports the trading path as unobserved when this is absent—it never promotes a
# provider-only snapshot to nominal. In local development an empty URL falls
# back to http://127.0.0.1:8000.
ALPHAENGINE_GATEWAY_URL=
ALPHAENGINE_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# Optional build-time Ed25519 private key. First pin its public-key SPKI SHA-256
# fingerprint in lib/artifact-trust.mjs. next.config.mjs then uses the private
# key only while building to sign the content-addressed provenance digest; it is
# never compiled into the app. Without both the reviewed trust root and this
# signer, Artifact custody remains fail-closed.
# Generate a PEM with: openssl genpkey -algorithm ED25519
ALPHAENGINE_ARTIFACT_SIGNING_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Systems console — operator actions (POST /api/system/actions)
#
# Read-only telemetry (GET /api/system/health|events|inspect) never needs this.
# The WRITE path does: purging a cache is refilled with live quota, a health
# probe spends a call, and resetting a ledger can let an instance overspend a
# vendor's real allowance. So:
#
#   set    → every action must present `Authorization: Bearer <this value>`
#   unset  → open outside production, and REFUSED (503) in production
#
# Being unset is therefore safe by default on a public deployment, and the
# console shows the reason instead of offering buttons that would 503.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
ALPHAENGINE_OPERATOR_TOKEN=

# Optional, exact-match paper-order convenience for a public demo. When set to
# 1 alongside ALPHAENGINE_OPERATOR_TOKEN, POST /api/gateway/orders may use the
# server-held token only when the browser sends no Authorization header. A
# pasted token is a strict override; risk controls and remediation stay gated.
ALPHAENGINE_PAPER_ORDER_DEFAULT=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Oracle Autonomous Database 23ai — vector research search + in-database VaR
#
# Optional, like every key above. Unset is safe and is the default for the
# public demo: the Research similarity panel and the Risk tab's Oracle VaR read
# "unavailable" rather than showing an empty result, and nothing else changes.
#
# Walletless TLS, so no cwallet.sso is needed anywhere — use the tcps
# descriptor on port 1521 from OCI → Autonomous Database → DB Connection, with
# mutual TLS DISABLED. Prefer the _low or _tp service over _high: a serverless
# deployment opens a pool per warm instance, and the low-concurrency service is
# the one sized for that.
ORACLE_CONN_STRING=
ORACLE_PASSWORD=

# Defaults to ADMIN so the credentials from the OCI provisioning screen work
# with nothing else set. ADMIN is a DBA, though, and this variable is readable
# by anything running in the deployment — run `oracle/03_app_user.sql` and set
# this to ALPHAENGINE_APP before any public deploy. That user has SELECT on one
# table, EXECUTE on one procedure, and no tablespace quota.
ORACLE_USER=

# Mutual TLS, and needed only while the database requires it.
#
# An Autonomous Database permits walletless TLS only once it has a network ACL
# or a private endpoint. With "secure access from everywhere" — the default —
# Oracle forces mutual TLS, and then these two are the difference between the
# Oracle panels working and reading "unavailable".
#
# ORACLE_WALLET_PEM_B64 is base64 of `ewallet.pem` from the wallet zip, and
# nothing else from that zip is used: thin mode reads the PEM alone.
#
#   Database connection -> Download wallet, then
#   unzip -p wallet.zip ewallet.pem | base64 | tr -d '\n' | pbcopy
#
# The PEM contains a private key. Set it as an environment variable, never in
# the repository, and rotate it by downloading a new wallet.
#
# Unset is safe: the client connects walletless, which is correct for a database
# that has an ACL and mutual TLS turned off.
ORACLE_WALLET_PEM_B64=
ORACLE_WALLET_PASSWORD=

# Apply the schema once per database:
#   sqlplus ADMIN/"$ORACLE_PASSWORD"@"$ORACLE_CONN_STRING" @oracle/01_schema.sql
#   sqlplus ADMIN/"$ORACLE_PASSWORD"@"$ORACLE_CONN_STRING" @oracle/02_monte_carlo.sql
# Then verify from this directory:  node scripts/verify-oracle.mjs

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase — the live decision tape (browser realtime)
#
# PUBLIC by design, and narrow by policy. `NEXT_PUBLIC_` means these ship in the
# browser bundle, so read what the anon key can actually reach before setting
# them: `supabase/migrations/20260808120700_anon_demo_realtime.sql` grants anon
# SELECT on gateway-decided, unowned rows of the public demo desk and nothing
# else. Risk limits stay closed; the sandbox rows stay excluded; there is no
# INSERT, UPDATE or DELETE.
#
# Unset is safe and is the default: the Execution tab's decision tape reads
# "not configured in this deployment" and every other surface is unchanged, as
# the gateway's DuckDB blotter remains authoritative either way.
#
# These two now carry a second surface: the optional sign-in at /login. Unset
# still means unset — the login page says authentication is not configured in
# this deployment and the workspace is unchanged, because nothing is gated
# behind an account.
#
# NEVER put the service-role key here. It belongs only in the gateway's .env.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Telegram companion — the header's Telegram button
#
# PUBLIC by design: a bot username is public information the moment the bot
# exists, and `NEXT_PUBLIC_` means it ships in the browser bundle. The username
# only, never the token — the bot token lives in the gateway's .env and nowhere
# else.
#
# Unset is safe and is the default: the header button does not render at all.
# That is deliberate. A placeholder would produce a t.me link that 404s, which
# is worse than an absent affordance — the button would be lying.
#
# Set it to the username without the @, e.g. AlphaEngineDeskBot. The link opens
# https://t.me/<username>?start=auth in a new tab; the gateway's /start handler
# accepts the payload and answers with its command card.
#
# Vercel note: this is read at build time by static substitution, so changing it
# in the dashboard does nothing until the next deployment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME=
